# Installation

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/parametric-curve-parameter-estimation.git
```

Navigate to the project directory:

```bash
cd parametric-curve-parameter-estimation
```

Install the dependencies:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

# Running the Project

## Jupyter Notebook

Start Jupyter:

```bash
jupyter notebook
```

Open:

```text
solution.ipynb
```

and run the cells sequentially.

## Python Script

Alternatively, run:

```bash
python main.py
```

The program will:

1. Load the dataset.
2. Define the parametric curve.
3. Estimate the unknown parameters.
4. Calculate the L1 loss.
5. Generate the fitted curve.
6. Display the comparison plot.
7. Save the final parameters.

---

# Conclusion

The unknown parameters of the given parametric curve were estimated using mathematical transformation and constrained nonlinear optimization.

The final estimated parameters are:

$$
\boxed{
\theta = 30^\circ,\quad
M = 0.03,\quad
X = 55
}
$$

The resulting parametric curve closely matches the supplied dataset.

